#!/usr/bin/python3 -IB
"""Claude Code PreToolUse hook (Bash): refuse a command that waits on CI, a pull request or a background job by
sleeping and checking again, or a `pkill -f` that kills its own shell. Part of fork-kit/agent-guards (README.md
there: install, settings entry, the machine file's "agent-guards" section).

Why: agents spent about 39% of their tool time in wait loops they wrote themselves (`for i in $(seq 1 40); do grep
-q DONE "$F" && break; sleep 30; done`, `while ! gh pr checks 12; do sleep 60; done`, `sleep 300; gh run view`).
Each loop overshoots the end by up to one sleep, it ends at the Bash timeout and is written again, and each new poll
is a model turn that sends the whole context again. The host has wait tools that wake the agent instead.

Refuses (a Bash call in the foreground) a loop that both checks such a state and sleeps, inside the same loop (its
condition counts), when it waits long; or a check after long top-level sleeps:
  a check   `gh run|pr|api|workflow|release ...`, curl/wget (to any URL: a GitHub one counts as a CI check), or a
            look at a file or a process: ls, stat, find, pgrep, pidof, ps, kill -0, a file test (`[ -f x ]`,
            `test -e`, `[[ -s x ]]`), and grep, rg, tail, head, cat, wc, jq when they do not read a pipe;
  waits     a while or until loop with no counter waits without end when a round sleeps loopSleepSeconds (default
            5) or more, and for a CI check with any sleep at all; a loop with rounds (`for x in a b c`, `$(seq 1
            40)`, `{1..40}`, a counter test `[ $n -lt 3 ]` or `(( n < 3 ))`) when its sleeps add up to more than
            maxSleepSeconds (default 120; a count it cannot read is one round); top-level sleeps over that, then a
            check (`sleep 300; gh run view 1`);
  or        `gh run watch`, `gh pr checks --watch`, and `watch -n N <check>` (a loop of N s rounds).
Lets through: a retry loop (a command tried again after a sleep, with no check inside that loop, even when the same
call reads a file before or after it), short waits (a loop of 1 s sleeps for a local server, a few rounds that stay
under the limit), a sleep with no check after it, a counter test (`[ $n -lt 3 ]` is a bound, not a check), any
command run in the background (`run_in_background`: the host wakes the agent when it ends), and text that only names
these (echo, a commit message, a heredoc into a file, a comment; a quoted "#1150" is no comment).
Also lets through a wait on the agent's OWN background job, in the foreground too (bg-guard refuses to let the turn
end while that job runs, and tells the agent to wait for it: the two must agree): a loop whose every check is one of a
few exact forms that read only that job, and nothing else beside it (Own, Reading._own_call):
  its output file  `[ -s|-f|-e|-r F ]` (test, [, [[, `!` allowed, one test each), or grep/tail/head/cat/wc/ls/stat
            with options from a short list (OWN_READ) on F and /dev/null; F is Claude Code's file of a
            run_in_background command, `<tmp>/claude-<uid>/<project>/<session id>/tasks/<task>.output` with no
            symlink on the way, written out or through a variable set once (`f=F; until [ -s "$f" ]; ...`);
  its process      `kill -0 <pid>..`, `ps -p <pid>` (with -o/-h only), `[ -d /proc/<pid> ]` (that folder itself),
            `tail --pid=<pid>`, for a process in the agent's own Claude Code process tree or `$!` of a job the same
            command started; in a `while` loop's own condition also a PID that names no process now (the job
            bg-guard named has ended: `while kill -0 A || kill -0 B` then ends at once, not refused).
Anything else stays refused: another session's or user's file, a process outside that tree, another selector or
input (`ps -e`, `grep x - < f`, `[[ own || other ]]`), find (-exec), rg (--pre), jq, a value set twice, in a branch,
a subshell or for one command only. And a Monitor: Claude Code runs a Monitor call's command through the Bash hooks
with tool_name "Bash", so the guard looks the call's tool_use_id up in the transcript (its tail, for up to
MONITOR_LOOK seconds, only when it found a wait: the line may be written just after the hook starts). A Monitor with
an until-condition on a file or a process is the right way to wait (it streams, it is no model turn per check), so
it passes; a Monitor that polls CI, a pull request or anything else outside this machine (gh, a curl/wget to any URL
but localhost/127.x/[::1]) is refused like a Bash loop. A call it cannot find there counts as Bash (refused as
before). Shell text handed on (`bash -c '..'`, `sh -c`, `sudo -u x bash -c`, `eval`, `bash <<EOF`, `cat <<EOF | bash`)
is read the same way (a value set inside it is not kept).
Known gaps (misses, on purpose: a false refusal costs more): a count it cannot read (`$(seq 1 $N)`, `[ $n -lt $MAX
]`, C-style `for ((..))`) is one round; a script file it does not open; a loop built with a function. Its own-job
test is narrow the other way (it refuses what it cannot prove is the agent's own): a PID from `$(cat x.pid)` or
pgrep, a relative path, an option off its list, a PID of an ended job outside `while <cond>` or one that another
process took again. One the other way: a value set outside `bash -c '...'` counts inside it, although single-quoted
text there sees it only when it is exported (the guard reads no quotes; at worst it waits on a file of nobody).
Also refuses (foreground or background: F7, 107 calls in two weeks) a `pkill -f P`, `kill $(pgrep -f P)` or `pgrep -f
P | xargs kill` whose pattern also matches this command's text: the host runs the command as `bash -c '<text>'`, so
that shell's command line matches too, pkill spares only itself, and the shell dies (exit 143/144, nothing after it
runs). Lets through -x, -A (--ignore-ancestors), -v, -F, no -f, and a pattern from a variable (not read: a gap).
Settings (machine file, pollLoop): enabled (default true), maxSleepSeconds (120), loopSleepSeconds (5).
Fail open: a broken settings part, a lib that cannot load, broken input or its own error lets the command run, with
one line saying so. Exit 2 (refuse) only answers a wait it found. Tests: fork-kit/agent-guards/tests/poll-loop.test.py
"""
import json, math, os, re, shlex, sys, time

NAME = 'poll-loop-guard'
DEFAULTS = {'enabled': True, 'maxSleepSeconds': 120, 'loopSleepSeconds': 5}


def _settings():
    """(pollLoop settings, problem or None). A problem means the guard lets every call through (never blocks on a
    broken config)."""
    try:
        sys.path.insert(0, os.path.join(os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(os.path.realpath(__file__))), 'lib'))
        from agent_guards import config
        return config.load('pollLoop')
    except BaseException as e:   # noqa: BLE001 - fail open
        return dict(DEFAULTS), f'cannot load the kit\'s config code ({type(e).__name__}: {e})'


OPS = ('&&', '||', ';;', '|&', '>>', '<<', ';', '&', '|', '(', ')', '<', '>', '\n')
PUNCT = set('();<>|&\n')
SEPARATORS = {'&&', '||', ';;', '|&', ';', '&', '|', '(', ')', '\n'}
KEYWORDS = {'then', 'do', 'else', 'elif', 'if', '!', '{', '}', 'time'}
# wrappers that run the command after them, with the options of theirs that take a value
WRAPPERS = {'sudo': {'-u', '-g', '-C', '-D', '-h', '-p', '-r', '-t', '-U', '-T', '--user', '--group', '--host',
                     '--prompt', '--chdir', '--role', '--type', '--other-user', '--command-timeout', '--close-from'},
            'env': {'-u', '-C', '--unset', '--chdir'}, 'nice': {'-n', '--adjustment'},
            'ionice': {'-c', '-n', '-p', '-P', '-u', '--class', '--classdata'}, 'stdbuf': {'-i', '-o', '-e'},
            'timeout': {'-s', '-k', '--signal', '--kill-after'},
            'nohup': set(), 'command': set(), 'builtin': set(), 'exec': {'-a'}, 'setsid': set(), 'heavy': set(),
            'chronic': set(), 'unbuffer': set()}
SHELLS = {'bash', 'sh', 'zsh', 'dash', 'ksh'}
LOOKS = {'ls', 'stat', 'find', 'pgrep', 'pidof', 'ps'}            # always a look at a file or a process
READERS = {'grep', 'egrep', 'fgrep', 'rg', 'tail', 'head', 'cat', 'wc', 'jq'}   # a look, unless they read a pipe
TESTS = {'test', '[', '[['}
FILE_TESTS = {'-e', '-f', '-s', '-d', '-p', '-r', '-w', '-x', '-L', '-h', '-S', '-b', '-c', '-N', '-O', '-G', '-nt',
              '-ot', '-ef'}
NUMBER_TESTS = {'-lt', '-le', '-gt', '-ge', '-eq', '-ne'}
COUNTER_TESTS = {'-lt', '-le', '-gt', '-ge'}     # a counter; -eq/-ne test a status, never a bound
GH_CHECKS = {'run', 'pr', 'api', 'workflow', 'release'}
WATCH_FLAGS_WITH_VALUE = {'-n', '--interval', '-q', '--equexit', '-s', '--shell'}
HEREDOC = re.compile(r'<<(-?)\s*(["\']?)([A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*)\2')
INTO_SHELL = re.compile(r'\|\s*(?:sudo\s+(?:-\S+\s+)*)?(?:\S*/)?(?:bash|sh|zsh|dash|ksh)\b')
COUNTER = re.compile(r'\$\{?[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*\}?|[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*|-?\d+')
DEPTH = 8
OWN_BG = '\x00bg'            # `$!` after a `&` in the same command: a job this command starts itself
OWN_LIST = {'export', 'local', 'declare', 'readonly', 'typeset'}   # assignments as arguments
VAR = re.compile(r'\$\{(!|[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*)\}|\$(!|[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*)')
SESSION = re.compile(r'[A-Za-z0-9-]{8,128}')
TOOL_USE_ID = re.compile(r'[A-Za-z0-9_-]{1,128}')
MONITOR_LOOK = 1.5           # seconds to look for the tool_use line in the transcript (only when a wait was found)
TRANSCRIPT_TAIL = 1 << 20    # bytes of the transcript's end that are read
CLAUDE = 'claude'            # Claude Code's process name (as bg-guard)
LOCAL_URL = re.compile(r'(?:[a-z][a-z0-9+.-]*://)?(?:[^/@\s]*@)?(?:localhost|127(?:\.\d{1,3}){3}|\[::1\]|0\.0\.0\.0)'
                       r'(?::\d+)?(?:[/?#].*)?', re.I)
HOST = re.compile(r'[A-Za-z0-9-]+(?:\.[A-Za-z0-9-]+)+(?::\d+)?(?:/.*)?')
CURL_ELSEWHERE = {'-x', '--proxy', '--preproxy', '--resolve', '--connect-to', '-K', '--config', '--socks5',
                  '--socks5-hostname', '--socks4', '--socks4a'}
# the exact forms a check of the agent's own job may take (anything else in such a call: not its own)
OWN_TEST_FILE = {'-e', '-f', '-s', '-r'}
OWN_TEST_PROC = {'-d', '-e'}
OWN_READ = {   # command: (short option letters, options with a value, long options)
    'grep': (set('qsFEGixwlcvaHhn'), {'-e', '-m'}, {'--quiet', '--silent', '--count', '--fixed-strings',
                                                    '--extended-regexp', '--ignore-case', '--no-filename'}),
    'tail': (set('fFqv'), {'-n', '-c'}, {'--follow', '--quiet', '--silent'}),
    'head': (set('qv'), {'-n', '-c'}, {'--quiet', '--silent'}),
    'cat': (set('AbeEnstTuv'), set(), set()),
    'wc': (set('lcwmL'), set(), {'--lines', '--bytes', '--words', '--chars'}),
    'ls': (set('laAhs1dtrSi'), set(), set()),
    'stat': (set('Lt'), {'-c'}, set()),
}
OWN_READ['egrep'] = OWN_READ['fgrep'] = OWN_READ['grep']
# pkill/pgrep (procps): the options that take a value (short, then long without "=")
KILL_SHORT_VALUE = set('gGPstuUFrqOd')
KILL_LONG_VALUE = {'--signal', '--group', '--parent', '--pgroup', '--session', '--terminal', '--euid', '--uid',
                   '--runstates', '--older', '--queue', '--ns', '--nslist', '--delimiter', '--cgroup', '--env',
                   '--pidfile'}
KILL_LONG_FLAG = {'--full': 'f', '--exact': 'x', '--ignore-ancestors': 'A', '--inverse': 'v', '--ignore-case': 'i'}
SIGNALS = set('HUP INT QUIT ILL TRAP ABRT IOT BUS FPE KILL USR1 SEGV USR2 PIPE ALRM TERM STKFLT CHLD CONT STOP TSTP '
              'TTIN TTOU URG XCPU XFSZ VTALRM PROF WINCH IO POLL PWR SYS'.split())
POSIX_CLASSES = {'alpha': 'a-zA-Z', 'digit': '0-9', 'alnum': 'a-zA-Z0-9', 'upper': 'A-Z', 'lower': 'a-z',
                 'space': r' \t\n\r\f\v', 'blank': r' \t', 'punct': r'!-/:-@\[-`{-~', 'xdigit': '0-9A-Fa-f',
                 'word': r'\w', 'print': r' -~', 'graph': '!-~', 'cntrl': r'\x00-\x1f\x7f'}


def kill_pattern(args):
    """The -f pattern of a pkill/pgrep call that also matches the shell running it, as text, or None: no -f, no
    pattern, a pattern from a variable, or -x/-A/-v/-F (these do not match their own shell the same way)."""
    flags, pattern, args = set(), None, list(args)
    if args and (args[0][1:].isdigit() or args[0][1:].upper().removeprefix('SIG') in SIGNALS) and args[0][:1] == '-':
        args.pop(0)                                    # pkill -9 / -KILL / -SIGTERM
    while args:
        a = args.pop(0)
        if a == '--':
            pattern = pattern if pattern is not None else (args[0] if args else None)
            break
        if a.startswith('--'):
            name = a.partition('=')[0]
            flags.add(KILL_LONG_FLAG.get(name, ''))
            if name == '--pidfile':
                flags.add('F')
            if name in KILL_LONG_VALUE and '=' not in a and args:
                args.pop(0)
        elif a.startswith('-') and len(a) > 1:
            for k, c in enumerate(a[1:]):
                flags.add(c)
                if c in KILL_SHORT_VALUE:
                    if k + 2 == len(a) and args:
                        args.pop(0)
                    break
        elif pattern is None:
            pattern = a
    if 'f' not in flags or flags & {'x', 'A', 'v', 'F'} or not pattern or re.search(r'\$[\w{(@*#?!-]', pattern):
        return None
    return pattern, 'i' in flags


def matches_own_shell(pattern, ignore_case, command):
    """True when the ERE also matches the command line of the shell that runs this command: `bash -c '<text>'`
    (the host hands the text to a shell; a quote in it may come out as '\\'')."""
    import warnings
    ere = re.sub(r'\[:(\w+):\]', lambda m: POSIX_CLASSES.get(m.group(1), m.group(0)), pattern)
    try:
        with warnings.catch_warnings():
            warnings.simplefilter('ignore')
            rx = re.compile(ere, re.S | (re.I if ignore_case else 0))
    except (re.error, RecursionError, OverflowError):
        return False                                    # a pattern we cannot read: not ours to judge
    return any(rx.search(f'/bin/bash -c {text} ;') for text in (command, command.replace("'", "'\\''")))


def strip_heredocs(text):
    """The text without the bodies of heredocs that go to anything but a shell (a brief written to a file is text,
    not commands); a heredoc into bash or sh (`bash <<EOF`, `cat <<EOF | bash`) keeps its body, read as commands."""
    out, lines, i = [], text.split('\n'), 0
    while i < len(lines):
        line = lines[i]
        out.append(line)
        i += 1
        for m in HEREDOC.finditer(line):
            before = line[:m.start()].split()
            if before and os.path.basename(before[-1]) in SHELLS or INTO_SHELL.search(line[m.end():]):
                continue
            tabs, delim = m.group(1), m.group(3)
            while i < len(lines) and (lines[i].lstrip('\t') if tabs else lines[i]) != delim:
                i += 1
            i += 1
    return '\n'.join(out)


def strip_comments(text):
    """The text without its shell comments: a # that starts a word, outside quotes, to the end of its line (a quoted
    "#1150" is a word, not a comment)."""
    out, i, n, quote, prev = [], 0, len(text), None, '\n'
    while i < n:
        c = text[i]
        if quote:
            if c == '\\' and quote == '"' and i + 1 < n:
                out.append(c + text[i + 1])
                i += 2
                continue
            if c == quote:
                quote = None
        elif c == '\\' and i + 1 < n:
            out.append(c + text[i + 1])
            prev = text[i + 1]
            i += 2
            continue
        elif c in '\'"':
            quote = c
        elif c == '#' and prev in ' \t\n;&|()':
            j = text.find('\n', i)
            if j < 0:
                break
            i = j
            continue
        out.append(c)
        prev = c
        i += 1
    return ''.join(out)


def backticks(text):
    """`cmd` as $(cmd), outside single quotes, so one reader handles both (an unquoted one splits into words)."""
    out, quote, open_ = [], None, False
    for k, c in enumerate(text):
        if c == "'" and not open_ and quote != '"' and (k == 0 or text[k - 1] != '\\'):
            quote = None if quote == "'" else "'"
        elif c == '"' and quote != "'" and (k == 0 or text[k - 1] != '\\'):
            quote = None if quote == '"' else '"'
        elif c == '`' and quote != "'" and (k == 0 or text[k - 1] != '\\'):
            out.append(')' if open_ else '$(')
            open_ = not open_
            continue
        out.append(c)
    return ''.join(out)


def tokens(text):
    lex = shlex.shlex(backticks(strip_comments(strip_heredocs(text))), posix=True, punctuation_chars='();<>|&\n')
    lex.whitespace, lex.commenters, lex.whitespace_split = ' \t\r', '', True
    out = []
    for t in lex:
        if t and set(t) <= PUNCT:
            while t:
                op = next(o for o in OPS + (t[0],) if t.startswith(o))
                t = t[len(op):]
                out.append(op)
        else:
            out.append(t)
    return out


def seconds(word, unknown):
    if word == 'infinity':
        return math.inf
    m = re.fullmatch(r'(\d+(?:\.\d*)?|\.\d+)([smhd]?)', word)
    if not m:
        return unknown
    return float(m.group(1)) * {'': 1, 's': 1, 'm': 60, 'h': 3600, 'd': 86400}[m.group(2)]


def rounds(words):
    """The rounds of a for loop's list, or 1 when it cannot be counted."""
    text = ' '.join(words)
    m = re.fullmatch(r'\{(-?\d+)\.\.(-?\d+)(?:\.\.(-?\d+))?\}', text)
    if m:
        a, b, step = int(m.group(1)), int(m.group(2)), abs(int(m.group(3) or 1)) or 1
        return abs(b - a) // step + 1
    m = re.fullmatch(r'(?:\$ \( |`)seq (-?\d+)(?: (-?\d+))?(?: (-?\d+))?(?: \)|`)', text)
    if m:
        nums = [int(g) for g in m.groups() if g is not None]
        a, step, b = (1, 1, nums[0]) if len(nums) == 1 else (nums[0], 1, nums[1]) if len(nums) == 2 else nums
        return max(0, (b - a) // step + 1) if step else 1
    if words and all(re.fullmatch(r'[A-Za-z0-9_.,:/+=@%-]+', w) for w in words):
        return len(words)
    return 1


def frame(kind, n=1):
    """One loop being read (or the top): its rounds, the sleep of one round, and the checks made inside it."""
    return {'kind': kind, 'n': n, 'sleep': 0.0, 'ci': [], 'local': [], 'bound': None, 'cond': kind == 'while'}


def substitutions(word):
    """The command texts inside `$(...)` of one word (`"$(gh pr view 5 -q .state)"` is one word to the shell
    reader, and its inside runs as commands; backticks are $(...) by then)."""
    out, i = [], 0
    while i < len(word):
        if word.startswith('$(', i) and not word.startswith('$((', i):
            depth, j = 1, i + 2
            while j < len(word) and depth:
                depth += {'(': 1, ')': -1}.get(word[j], 0)
                j += 1
            out.append(word[i + 2:j - 1] if not depth else word[i + 2:])
            i = j
        else:
            i += 1
    return out


def pinned(text):
    """The names this command sets exactly once, by a plain `NAME=value` (or `export NAME=value`), and names nowhere
    else bare: no `for NAME`, `read NAME`, `NAME+=`, `NAME[..]`, `printf -v NAME`, `unset NAME`, `(( NAME++ ))`. Only
    these keep a value the guard can know (the text order is then the run order); any other name is not known."""
    seen, once = {}, set()
    for m in re.finditer(r'(?<![\w$-])(?<!\$\{)([A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*)(=)?', text):
        name = m.group(1)
        seen[name] = seen.get(name, 0) + 1
        if m.group(2) and not text.startswith('==', m.start(2)):
            once.add(name)
    return {n for n in once if seen[n] == 1 and not re.search(r'-v\s*' + n + r'\b', text)}


def local_url(args):
    """A curl/wget that asks only this machine: a localhost/127.x/[::1] URL, no other URL or host name, and no
    option that sends it elsewhere (a proxy, --resolve, --connect-to, a config file)."""
    if any(a.split('=', 1)[0] in CURL_ELSEWHERE for a in args):
        return False
    words = [a for a in args if not a.startswith('-')]
    return any(LOCAL_URL.fullmatch(a) for a in words) and not any(
        ('://' in a or HOST.fullmatch(a)) and not LOCAL_URL.fullmatch(a) for a in words)


def _ppid(pid):
    try:
        with open(f'/proc/{pid}/stat') as f:
            return int(f.read().rsplit(')', 1)[1].split()[1])
    except (OSError, IndexError, ValueError):
        return 0


def _argv0(pid):
    try:
        with open(f'/proc/{pid}/cmdline', 'rb') as f:
            return os.path.basename(f.read().split(b'\0', 1)[0].decode(errors='replace'))
    except OSError:
        return ''


def claude_pid(start):
    """The Claude Code process above `start` (as bg-guard finds it), or 0."""
    pid, n = start, 0
    while pid > 1 and n < 64:
        if _argv0(pid) == CLAUDE:
            return pid
        pid, n = _ppid(pid), n + 1
    return 0


class Own:
    """What is the agent's own background job: the output file Claude Code writes for its run_in_background command
    (`<tmp>/claude-<uid>/<project>/<session id>/tasks/<task>.output`, `<tmp>` being /tmp, $TMPDIR or
    $CLAUDE_CODE_TMPDIR; the path as written must be the real one: no symlink in it), or a running process under its
    Claude Code process (not that process itself). `pid` is a test of a PID (the hook's: the process tree in /proc),
    `gone` one that the PID names no process at all; a session id that is empty or odd makes no file its own."""

    def __init__(self, session, pid=None, gone=None, roots=None, uid=None):
        self.session = session if isinstance(session, str) and SESSION.fullmatch(session) else ''
        self._pid = pid if pid is not None else self._tree
        self._gone = gone if gone is not None else (lambda n: not os.path.exists(f'/proc/{n}'))
        if roots is None:
            roots = ['/tmp'] + [os.environ.get(k, '') for k in ('TMPDIR', 'CLAUDE_CODE_TMPDIR')]
        self.roots = sorted({os.path.normpath(r) for r in roots if r and r.startswith('/')})
        self.uid = os.getuid() if uid is None else uid
        self._root = None

    def _tree(self, pid):
        if self._root is None:
            self._root = claude_pid(os.getppid())
        if not self._root or pid <= 1 or pid == self._root:
            return False
        p, n = pid, 0
        while p > 1 and n < 64:
            p, n = _ppid(p), n + 1
            if p == self._root:
                return True
        return False

    def pid(self, n):
        try:
            return bool(self._pid(n))
        except Exception:   # noqa: BLE001 - cannot tell: not its own
            return False

    def gone(self, n):
        try:
            return n > 1 and bool(self._gone(n))
        except Exception:   # noqa: BLE001 - cannot tell: not gone
            return False

    def proc(self, p):
        """`/proc/<pid>` itself (nothing under it: /proc/<pid>/root and cwd reach every file) of its own tree."""
        m = re.fullmatch(r'/proc/(\d+)/?', p)
        return bool(m) and self.pid(int(m.group(1)))

    def path(self, p):
        if not self.session or not p.startswith('/') or '$' in p or '`' in p or '\x00' in p:
            return False
        p = os.path.normpath(p)
        for root in self.roots:
            m = re.fullmatch(re.escape(root) + r'/claude-(\d+)/[^/]+/([^/]+)/tasks/[A-Za-z0-9_-]{1,64}\.output', p)
            if m and int(m.group(1)) == self.uid and m.group(2) == self.session:
                try:     # no symlink on the way: the file (when it is there) and its folders are where they say
                    return os.path.realpath(p) == os.path.join(os.path.realpath(root), os.path.relpath(p, root))
                except (OSError, ValueError):
                    return False
        return False


class Reading:
    """What one command does. A wait is a loop that both sleeps and checks inside the same loop (its condition
    counts), or a check after top-level sleeps. A check elsewhere in the command (an `ls` before a retry loop, a
    `cat` of its log after it) does not make a retry loop a wait."""

    def __init__(self, settings, text='', own=None, monitor=False):
        self.s = settings
        self.text = text       # the whole command: the shell that runs it has this on its command line
        self.own = own         # an Own, or None: nothing is the agent's own job
        self.monitor = monitor  # a Monitor's command: a curl to anything but this machine counts as CI
        self.pinned = pinned(text)   # the names whose value it may know
        self.vars = {}         # NAME -> its value as far as it is known (None: not known)
        self.bg = False        # a `&` was seen: `$!` is a job of this command
        self.plain = True      # the command being read runs for sure, in this shell (top level, after ; or &)
        self.negated = False   # the command being read has a `!` before it
        self.depth = 0         # ... and is in shell text handed on (bash -c, eval, $(..)) when > 0
        self._bang = False
        self.found = []        # (what it checks, why it is a wait, 'ci' or 'local')
        self.watch = []
        self.kills = []        # the pkill/pgrep calls that also kill the shell running them
        self.prev = None       # the command before this one (`pgrep -f x | xargs kill`)
        self.into_kill = 0     # inside `kill $(...)`
        self.top_slept = 0.0   # the plain sleeps at the top so far (not inside a loop)
        self.stack = [frame('top')]

    def _nested(self, text, depth):
        """Shell text handed on (bash -c, eval, $(..), watch): a value it sets is not kept (a child shell)."""
        saved = dict(self.vars)
        self.read(text, depth)
        self.vars = saved

    def read(self, text, depth=0):
        if depth > DEPTH:
            return
        ts, base = tokens(text), len(self.stack)
        i, at_cmd, piped = 0, True, False
        last, ifs, paren, dollar = None, 0, 0, 0    # the last separator; if/case, (..) and $(..) it is inside
        while i < len(ts):
            t = ts[i]
            if t == '(' and i + 1 < len(ts) and ts[i + 1] == '(' and not (i and ts[i - 1].endswith('$')):
                j = i + 2                      # (( n < 3 )): arithmetic; a comparison with a number bounds a loop
                while j + 1 < len(ts) and not (ts[j] == ')' and ts[j + 1] == ')'):
                    j += 1
                inner = ts[i + 2:j]
                if any(x in ('<', '>') for x in inner):
                    self._bound([x.lstrip('=') for x in inner])
                i, at_cmd, piped = j + 2, False, False
                continue
            if t in SEPARATORS:
                self.bg = self.bg or (t == '&' and not (i and ts[i - 1] in ('>', '<')))   # not 2>&1
                if t == '(':
                    paren += 1
                elif t == ')':
                    dollar, paren = (dollar - 1, paren) if dollar else (0, max(0, paren - 1))
                at_cmd, piped, last = True, t in ('|', '|&'), t
                i += 1
                continue
            if t in ('<', '>', '>>', '<<'):
                i += 2
                continue
            if not at_cmd:
                if t == '$' and i + 1 < len(ts) and ts[i + 1] == '(':
                    at_cmd, piped, dollar = True, False, dollar + 1
                    i += 2
                    continue
                i += 1
                continue
            word = os.path.basename(t) if '/' in t and not t.startswith('[') else t
            if word == 'do' and self.stack[-1]['kind'] == 'while':
                self.stack[-1]['cond'] = False         # the loop's own condition ends here
            plain = len(self.stack) == max(base, 1) and not ifs and not paren and last in (None, ';', '\n', '&')
            if word in ('if', 'case'):
                ifs += 1
            elif word in ('fi', 'esac'):
                ifs = max(0, ifs - 1)
            if word in KEYWORDS or re.fullmatch(r'[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*=.*', t, re.S):
                for inner in substitutions(t):         # p="$(gh pr checks 5)"
                    self._nested(inner, depth + 1)
                if word == '!':
                    self._bang = True
                elif word not in KEYWORDS:
                    j = i + 1                          # `f=x cmd`: a value for that command only
                    while j < len(ts) and re.fullmatch(r'[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*=.*', ts[j], re.S):
                        j += 1
                    prefix = j < len(ts) and ts[j] not in SEPARATORS and ts[j] not in ('<', '>', '>>', '<<')
                    self._assign(t, plain and not prefix)
                i += 1
                continue
            if word == '$' and i + 1 < len(ts) and ts[i + 1] == '(':
                dollar += 1
                i += 2
                continue
            if word in ('while', 'until'):
                self.stack.append(dict(frame('while', math.inf), word=word))
                i += 1
                continue
            if word == 'for':
                j = i + 1
                while j < len(ts) and ts[j] not in ('in', 'do', ';', '\n'):
                    j += 1
                words = []
                if j < len(ts) and ts[j] == 'in':
                    j += 1
                    while j < len(ts) and ts[j] not in (';', '\n', 'do'):
                        words.append(ts[j])
                        j += 1
                self.stack.append(frame('for', rounds(words) if words else 1))
                i = j
                continue
            if word == 'done' and len(self.stack) > base:
                self._close()
                i, at_cmd = i + 1, False
                continue
            args, j = [], i + 1
            while j < len(ts) and ts[j] not in SEPARATORS:
                args.append(ts[j])
                j += 1
            self.plain, self.negated, self.depth, self._bang = plain, self._bang, depth, False
            self._command(word, args, piped, depth)
            i, at_cmd = j, False
        while len(self.stack) > max(base, 1):
            self._close()

    def _expand(self, word):
        """The word with the variables it knows put in (`$!` after a `&`: OWN_BG); the others stay as written."""
        def put(m):
            name = m.group(1) or m.group(2)
            if name == '!':
                return OWN_BG if self.bg else m.group(0)
            value = self.vars.get(name)
            return m.group(0) if value is None else value
        return VAR.sub(put, word)

    def _assign(self, word, known=True):
        """A value it can know: set once in the whole command (pinned), where it runs for sure, not from $(..)."""
        name, _, value = word.partition('=')
        known = known and name in self.pinned and '$(' not in value and '`' not in value
        self.vars[name] = self._expand(value) if known else None

    def _own_pid(self, word):
        return word == OWN_BG or (word.isdigit() and self.own.pid(int(word)))

    def _ended(self, word):
        """A PID that names no process now, tested in a `while` loop's own condition (`while kill -0 A || kill -0 B`,
        the wait bg-guard names): that job has ended, so the test is false at once and ends the loop. In an `until`,
        after a `!`, in the body or in text handed on it would wait for some other process to take that PID."""
        f = self.stack[-1]
        return word.isdigit() and f.get('word') == 'while' and f['cond'] and not self.negated and \
            not self.depth and self.own.gone(int(word))

    def _own_call(self, word, args):
        """True when this check reads only the agent's own background job (Own), in one of a few exact forms:
        `kill -0 <pid>..`, `ps -p <pid>` (with -o/-h only), `[ -s|-f|-e|-r <own file> ]` or `[ -d|-e /proc/<pid> ]`
        (test, [ and [[ alike, one test each, `!` allowed), and grep/tail/head/cat/wc/ls/stat with options from a
        short list, its own files and /dev/null (`tail --pid=<pid>` too). Anything else (another selector, a file
        or input beside its own, an option it does not list, a value it does not know) is not its own, so the wait
        is judged as before."""
        if self.own is None:
            return False
        ex, k = [], 0
        while k < len(args):                     # without its redirections (`2>/dev/null`, `>out`)
            a = args[k]
            if a in ('<', '<<'):                 # it reads another input (`grep x - < /tmp/ci`): only /dev/null
                if a == '<<' or k + 1 >= len(args) or args[k + 1] != '/dev/null':
                    return False
                k += 2
                continue
            if a in ('>', '>>'):
                k += 2
                continue
            if len(a) == 1 and a.isdigit() and k + 1 < len(args) and args[k + 1] in ('<', '>', '>>'):   # 2>x
                k += 1
                continue
            ex.append(self._expand(a))
            k += 1
        if word == 'kill':
            pids = ex[1:] if ex[:1] == ['-0'] else []
            pids = pids[1:] if pids[:1] == ['--'] else pids
            return bool(pids) and all(self._own_pid(p) or self._ended(p) for p in pids)
        if word == 'ps':
            pids, k = [], 0
            while k < len(ex):
                a = ex[k]
                if a in ('-p', '--pid', '-q', '--quick-pid', '-o', '--format') and k + 1 < len(ex):
                    pids += ex[k + 1].split(',') if a not in ('-o', '--format') else []
                    k += 2
                    continue
                m = re.fullmatch(r'--(?:quick-)?pid=(.+)|-[pq](\d[\d,]*)', a)
                if m:
                    pids += (m.group(1) or m.group(2)).split(',')
                elif not re.fullmatch(r'-o.+|--format=.+|-h|--no-headers?', a):
                    return False                 # another selector (-e, -C, -u, --ppid) widens it to anyone
                k += 1
            return bool(pids) and all(self._own_pid(p) for p in pids)
        if word in TESTS:
            close = {'[': ']', '[[': ']]'}.get(word)
            if close and ex[-1:] != [close]:     # `[[ own || other ]]` reaches here split at the ||
                return False
            w = ex[:-1] if close else ex
            w = w[1:] if w[:1] == ['!'] else w
            return len(w) == 2 and ((w[0] in OWN_TEST_FILE and self.own.path(w[1])) or
                                    (w[0] in OWN_TEST_PROC and self.own.proc(w[1])))
        if word not in OWN_READ:                 # find (-exec), rg (--pre), jq, pgrep, curl ...: never its own
            return False
        letters, valued, longs = OWN_READ[word]
        number = re.compile(r'[+-]?\d+[kKmMbB]?')
        own, pattern, k = False, word in ('grep', 'egrep', 'fgrep'), 0
        while k < len(ex):
            a = ex[k]
            if a.startswith('--'):
                name, eq, val = a.partition('=')
                if word == 'tail' and name == '--pid':
                    if not self._own_pid(val):
                        return False
                    own = True
                elif not ((word in ('tail', 'head') and name in ('--lines', '--bytes') and number.fullmatch(val))
                          or (word == 'stat' and name in ('--format', '--printf') and '$' not in val)
                          or (not eq and name in longs)):
                    return False
            elif word in ('tail', 'head') and re.fullmatch(r'-\d+', a):
                pass
            elif a.startswith('-') and len(a) > 1:
                for j, c in enumerate(a[1:]):    # a cluster of short options; one with a value ends it (-n5)
                    if '-' + c in valued:
                        val = a[j + 2:]
                        if not val:
                            k += 1
                            val = ex[k] if k < len(ex) else '$'
                        if '$' in val or (c != 'c' or word != 'stat') and not number.fullmatch(val):
                            return False
                        break
                    if c not in letters:
                        return False
            elif pattern:                        # grep's pattern: its first other word
                if '$' in a:
                    return False
                pattern = False
            elif a == '/dev/null':
                pass
            elif self.own.path(a):
                own = True
            else:
                return False
            k += 1
        return own

    def _in_loop(self):
        return len(self.stack) > 1

    def _sleep(self, amount):
        if self._in_loop():
            self.stack[-1]['sleep'] += amount
        else:
            self.top_slept += amount

    def _check(self, kind, name):
        if kind == 'own':      # a look at the agent's own background job: waiting for it is the way bg-guard asks
            return
        if self._in_loop():
            self.stack[-1][kind].append(name)
        if self.top_slept > self.s['maxSleepSeconds']:
            slept = 'without end' if math.isinf(self.top_slept) else f'{self.top_slept:g} s'
            self.found.append((name, f'it sleeps {slept} first (more than {self.s["maxSleepSeconds"]} s), then '
                                     'checks', kind))

    def _bound(self, words):
        """A counter test (`[ $n -lt 3 ]`, `(( n < 3 ))`) in a while/until loop's own condition (not its body: a
        `[ "$p" -eq 0 ] && break` there is a status test) bounds that loop: its number is the rounds, one round when
        it is not a plain number; a 0 is no bound (`[ $pending -gt 0 ]` waits for a count to drop)."""
        f = self.stack[-1]
        if f['kind'] != 'while' or not f['cond']:
            return
        nums = [abs(int(w)) for w in words if re.fullmatch(r'-?\d+', w)]
        n = max(nums) if nums else 1
        if n:
            f['bound'] = max(f['bound'] or 0, n)

    def _close(self):
        f = self.stack.pop()
        up = self.stack[-1]
        n = f['bound'] if f['kind'] == 'while' and f['bound'] is not None else f['n']
        checks = sorted(set(f['ci'] + f['local']))
        kind = 'ci' if f['ci'] else 'local'
        if checks and f['sleep'] > 0:
            if math.isinf(n):
                if f['sleep'] >= self.s['loopSleepSeconds'] or f['ci']:
                    self.found.append((', '.join(checks), f'it loops with no end, sleeping {f["sleep"]:g} s a round',
                                       kind))
            elif f['sleep'] * n > self.s['maxSleepSeconds']:
                total = 'without end' if math.isinf(f['sleep']) else f'{f["sleep"] * n:g} s'
                self.found.append((', '.join(checks), f'its sleeps add up to {total} (more than '
                                                      f'{self.s["maxSleepSeconds"]} s)', kind))
        if len(self.stack) > 1:
            up['sleep'] += f['sleep'] * n if f['sleep'] else 0
        up['ci'] += f['ci']
        up['local'] += f['local']

    def _self_kill(self, word, args, tail=''):
        found = kill_pattern(args)
        if found and matches_own_shell(*found, self.text):
            self.kills.append((f'{word} -f {shlex.quote(found[0])}{tail}', found[0]))

    def _command(self, word, args, piped, depth):
        """Notes the sleep and the checks of one simple command, and reads text it hands to a shell."""
        while word in WRAPPERS:
            takes = WRAPPERS[word]
            while args and (args[0].startswith('-') or re.fullmatch(r'[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*=.*', args[0], re.S)):
                a = args.pop(0)
                if a == '--':
                    break
                if a in takes and args:
                    args.pop(0)
            if word == 'timeout' and args:
                args = args[1:]                # its duration
            if not args:
                return
            word, args = os.path.basename(args[0]), args[1:]
        if word in OWN_LIST:                   # `declare -n f=..` (a reference) and the like: not known
            options = any(a.startswith(('-', '+')) for a in args)
            for a in args:
                if re.fullmatch(r'[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*=.*', a, re.S):
                    self._assign(a, self.plain and not options)
        prev, kills = self.prev, word == 'kill' and not {'-0', '-s0', '--signal=0'} & set(args)
        if word not in SHELLS and word not in ('eval', 'watch'):
            self.into_kill += kills                # kill $(pgrep -f x): that pgrep feeds a kill
            for a in args:                         # [ "$(gh pr view 5 -q .state)" = OPEN ]: its inside runs too
                if '$(' in a:
                    for inner in substitutions(a):
                        self._nested(inner, depth + 1)
            self.into_kill -= kills
        self.prev = (word, args)
        fed = prev and prev[0] == 'kill' and prev[1][-1:] == ['$'] and not {'-0', '-s0'} & set(prev[1])
        if word == 'pkill' or (word == 'pgrep' and (self.into_kill or fed)):   # kill "$(pgrep ..)" / kill $(pgrep ..)
            self._self_kill(word, args)
        elif word == 'xargs' and piped and prev and prev[0] == 'pgrep' and \
                any(os.path.basename(a) == 'kill' for a in args) and '-0' not in args:
            self._self_kill('pgrep', prev[1], ' | xargs kill')
        if word == 'sleep':
            self._sleep(sum(seconds(a, self.s['loopSleepSeconds']) for a in args if not a.startswith('-')) or 0)
        elif word in SHELLS:
            for k, a in enumerate(args):
                if re.fullmatch(r'-[a-z]*c[a-z]*', a) and k + 1 < len(args):
                    self._nested(args[k + 1], depth + 1)
                    break
        elif word == 'eval':
            self._nested(' '.join(args), depth + 1)
        elif word == 'watch':              # `watch -n 60 gh pr checks 1`: a loop with its interval as the sleep
            interval = 2.0
            while args and args[0].startswith('-'):
                a = args.pop(0)
                if a in ('-n', '--interval') and args:
                    interval = seconds(args.pop(0), interval)
                elif a.startswith('--interval='):
                    interval = seconds(a.partition('=')[2], interval)
                elif re.fullmatch(r'-n\d+(?:\.\d*)?', a):
                    interval = seconds(a[2:], interval)
                elif a in WATCH_FLAGS_WITH_VALUE and args:
                    args.pop(0)
            if args:
                self.stack.append(frame('while', math.inf))
                self._sleep(interval)
                self._nested(' '.join(shlex.quote(a) if len(args) > 1 else a for a in args), depth + 1)
                self._close()
        elif word == 'gh':
            sub = [a for a in args if not a.startswith('-')]
            if sub and sub[0] in GH_CHECKS:
                if sub[:2] == ['run', 'watch'] or (sub[:2] == ['pr', 'checks'] and
                                                   any(a == '--watch' or a.startswith('--watch=') for a in args)):
                    self.watch.append('gh ' + ' '.join(sub[:2]))
                self._check('ci', 'gh ' + ' '.join(sub[:2]))
        elif word in ('curl', 'wget'):         # in a Monitor, any curl that is not to this machine is external
            ci = any('github.com' in a for a in args) or (self.monitor and not local_url(args))
            self._check('ci' if ci else 'local', word)
        elif word == 'kill':
            if '-0' in args:
                self._check('own' if self._own_call(word, args) else 'local', 'kill -0')
        elif word in TESTS:
            if any(a in FILE_TESTS for a in args):
                self._check('own' if self._own_call(word, args) else 'local', word)
            elif any(a in COUNTER_TESTS for a in args):
                k = next(k for k, a in enumerate(args) if a in COUNTER_TESTS)
                if k and k + 1 < len(args) and COUNTER.fullmatch(args[k - 1]) and COUNTER.fullmatch(args[k + 1]):
                    self._bound([args[k - 1], args[k + 1]])
        elif word in LOOKS or (word in READERS and not piped):
            self._check('own' if self._own_call(word, args) else 'local', word)


def verdict(command, settings, background=False, own=None, monitor=False):
    """None, or (what it checks, why it counts as a wait, 'ci' or 'local'), or (the call, its pattern, 'kill') for a
    pkill/pgrep that kills its own shell. A background command is only checked for that (the host wakes the agent
    when it ends, so a wait there is fine; a self-kill is not). `own` (an Own): checks of the agent's own background
    job are no wait. `monitor`: the command is a Monitor's, where only a wait on CI counts."""
    r = Reading(settings, command, own, monitor)
    r.read(command)
    if r.kills:
        return r.kills[0][0], r.kills[0][1], 'kill'
    if background:
        return None
    if r.watch:
        return ', '.join(sorted(set(r.watch))), 'it waits for CI to finish', 'ci'
    found = [f for f in r.found if f[2] == 'ci'] if monitor else r.found
    if not found:
        return None
    return next((f for f in found if f[2] == 'ci'), found[0])


def tool_of(event, wait=MONITOR_LOOK):
    """The name of the tool that made this call, from its tool_use line in the transcript (Claude Code runs a
    Monitor's command through the Bash hooks as tool_name "Bash"), or None: no id, no transcript, or no line in its
    last TRANSCRIPT_TAIL bytes within `wait` seconds (the line may be written just after the hook starts)."""
    tid, path = event.get('tool_use_id'), event.get('transcript_path')
    if not (isinstance(tid, str) and TOOL_USE_ID.fullmatch(tid) and isinstance(path, str) and path):
        return None
    rx = re.compile(rb'"id"\s*:\s*"' + re.escape(tid.encode()) + rb'"\s*,\s*"name"\s*:\s*"([A-Za-z0-9_.:-]{1,128})"')
    end = time.monotonic() + wait
    while True:
        try:
            with open(path, 'rb') as f:
                size = os.fstat(f.fileno()).st_size
                f.seek(max(0, size - TRANSCRIPT_TAIL))
                m = rx.search(f.read(TRANSCRIPT_TAIL))
            if m:
                return m.group(1).decode()
        except OSError:
            pass
        if time.monotonic() >= end:
            return None
        time.sleep(0.1)


def reason(what, why, kind, settings):
    if kind == 'kill':
        return (f'Refused by {NAME}: `{what}` also matches the shell that runs this command (its command line holds '
                'this text), so it kills that shell: exit 143/144 and nothing after it runs. Make the pattern miss its '
                "own text: bracket one letter (`pkill -f '[v]itest run'`, and don't name the process elsewhere in "
                'the same command), or kill by PID (`kill "$(cat run.pid)"`). Not refused: -x, -A '
                '(--ignore-ancestors), -F, or a pattern from a variable.')
    way = ('To wait for CI or a pull request: push and stop (or watch_pull_request); you are told when it ends.'
           if kind == 'ci' else
           'To wait for a job, a file or a process: run the job with run_in_background and wait with '
           't3_background_wait, or use Monitor with an until-condition; you are woken when it ends. A wait on your '
           'own background job (its PID, `while kill -0 <pid>; do sleep 30; done`, or its tasks/<id>.output file) '
           'is not refused.')
    return (f'Refused by {NAME}: this command waits by sleeping and checking again ({what}; {why}). Each new check '
            f'is a model turn that sends the whole context again, and the loop overshoots the end. {way} Not '
            'refused: a retry loop (a command tried again after a sleep, with no status check inside the loop), '
            f'and short waits (under {settings["maxSleepSeconds"]} s of sleep in all, or under '
            f'{settings["loopSleepSeconds"]} s a round in a local loop).')


def _first(text, event):
    """True when this session has not had this notice yet (the kit's lib; a lib that cannot load: always)."""
    try:
        from agent_guards import config
        return config.first_notice(text, event)
    except BaseException:   # noqa: BLE001
        return True


def _problem_out(problem, event):
    text = (f'{NAME}: the machine file\'s "agent-guards" section cannot be used as written ({problem}); built-in '
            f'defaults used for that part, and {NAME} lets every command through until it is fixed. Tell the owner; '
            '`agent-guards self-check` names every problem.')
    try:
        sys.stderr.write(text + '\n')
    except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001
        pass
    if not _first(text, event):
        return
    out = {'systemMessage': text}
    if isinstance(event, dict) and event.get('hook_event_name') == 'PreToolUse':
        out['hookSpecificOutput'] = {'hookEventName': 'PreToolUse', 'additionalContext': text}
    print(json.dumps(out))


def main(argv=None):
    """Exit 2 with the reason on stderr refuses; 0 lets the command run; 1 (this guard failed) lets it run, loudly."""
    argv = sys.argv[1:] if argv is None else argv
    if argv:
        sys.stderr.write(f'usage: {NAME} (hook: PreToolUse JSON on stdin; its settings entry: `agent-guards hooks`)\n')
        return 1
    event = None
    try:
        settings, problem = _settings()
        event = json.loads(sys.stdin.read())
        if problem:
            _problem_out(problem, event)
            return 0
        if not settings['enabled'] or not isinstance(event, dict) or event.get('tool_name') != 'Bash':
            return 0
        ti = event.get('tool_input') or {}
        command = ti.get('command')
        if not isinstance(command, str):
            return 0
        own = Own(event.get('session_id'))
        try:
            found = verdict(command, settings, ti.get('run_in_background') is True, own)
            if found and found[2] == 'local' and tool_of(event) == 'Monitor':
                found = verdict(command, settings, False, own, monitor=True)
        except ValueError:   # text a shell reader cannot split (an open quote): not ours to judge
            return 0
    except BaseException as e:   # noqa: BLE001 - fail open: this guards a habit, not an attack
        sys.stderr.write(f'{NAME}: failed ({type(e).__name__}: {e}); the command is NOT checked and runs. '
                         'Tell the owner if this repeats.\n')
        return 1
    if not found:
        return 0
    sys.stderr.write(reason(*found, settings) + '\n')
    return 2


if __name__ == '__main__':
    sys.exit(main())
